# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: install-core-builtins-leaks-com-hooks-across-suites — a test suite that installs the builtins breaks the cador suite run after it
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-install-core-builtins-leaks-com-hooks-across-suites

* Context

Found 2026-10-06 while adding exit-status tests to the clautolisp tool
suite (sysexits-exit-statuses.issue).

* Problem

=install-core-builtins= (autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp) SETFs
process-wide hooks: =*com-point-wrap-hook*=, =*com-point-unwrap-hook*=,
=*com-objects-wrap-hook*=, =*vlax-collection-items-hook*=,
=*resolve-unbound-function-hook*= and =*com-loaded-p*=. Once they are set,
COM point properties come back as VARIANT(SAFEARRAY) objects.

In =make -C clautolisp test-sbcl= the suites run in a fixed order: the
clautolisp tool suite, ..., the cador suite (1574 checks), then the
builtins suite. The cador suite expects plain lists from
=host-vlax-get-property ... "InsertionPoint"=, which it only gets because
no suite before it has installed the builtins. A tool-suite test that
calls =setup-context= (hence =install-core-builtins=) made 7 cador tests
fail with =#<VARIANT ARRAY #<SAFEARRAY>>= is not a LIST
(VLAX-BLOCK-ADDATTRIBUTE-ADDS-AN-ATTDEF-TO-THE-BLOCK,
INSERT-DELETE-ERASES-THE-ATTRIBUTE-RUN, ENTITY-MOVE-ROTATE-COPY-DELETE-METHODS,
INSERTBLOCK-*, ENTITY-PROPERTY-BRIDGE-READS-AND-WRITES-DXF-GROUPS). The
cador suite alone, and the full run on master, are green.

Repro: in =clautolisp/tools/clautolisp/tests/exit-status-tests.lisp=
remove the =with-isolated-builtin-hooks= wrapper and run =make -C
clautolisp test-sbcl=.

* Proposal

Either the cador tests bind the hooks they depend on (NIL, or the
host-level behaviour they test) instead of relying on the global default,
or =install-core-builtins= stops being process-global (hooks per session /
context). The exit-status tests work around it with
=with-isolated-builtin-hooks=, which rebinds the six variables.

* Acceptance criteria

- The cador suite passes when run after any suite that installs the
  builtins (e.g. move it after the builtins suite once, and see it stay
  green).

* Resolution (clautolisp 2.2.221, 2026-10-07)

** Reproduced

With the =with-isolated-builtin-hooks= wrapper removed from the tool
suite's exit-status tests, =make -C clautolisp test-sbcl= stops at the
cador suite with =Fail: 7= ("cador tests failed."). Also reproduced
directly: load the test systems, call =install-core-builtins=, then run
each perform-time suite: only the cador suite is affected (reader,
interactor, repl, source-map, runtime, drawing, host, cadtui and dcl stay
green with the hooks installed).

** Cause

The hooks are process-global on purpose -- once installed, the builtins
are the whole program's, and every production path installs them -- so
making them per-session would not help: the cador tests call the host
directly against the default context, which the other suites share too.
The order dependence came from the cador suite: it tests the host BELOW
the builtins layer (points as plain lists) but never established that
state; it inherited it from "no suite installed the builtins before me".
The tool suite runs at LOAD time (its run.lisp), i.e. before every
perform-time suite, so the first tool test that called =setup-context=
broke cador.

** Fix

- =clautolisp.autolisp-runtime:without-builtin-layer-hooks= (new,
  exported): binds every hook a layer above the runtime installs
  (=*resolve-unbound-function-hook*=, =*vlax-collection-items-hook*=,
  =*com-point-wrap-hook*=, =*com-point-unwrap-hook*=,
  =*com-objects-wrap-hook*=) to NIL for its body. It is the one list of
  those hooks; =install-core-builtins= carries a comment to keep the two
  in step.
- The cador suite runs inside =call-with-cador-suite-environment=
  (cador/tests/test-harness.lisp), which uses it: the suite now starts
  from a known hook state whatever ran before it.
- The tool suite's =with-isolated-builtin-hooks= workaround is removed.
  It is no longer needed, and without it the full run exercises the
  leaking order every time (the tool suite installs the builtins at load
  time, before cador).
- =*com-loaded-p*= is builtins-internal state that
  =install-core-builtins= resets itself; nothing below the builtins reads
  it, so it is not part of the bare-host state.

** Reproduction kept as tests

=autolisp-builtins-core/tests/builtin-hooks-isolation-tests.lisp= (the
builtins-core test system now depends on =clautolisp/cador/tests=):

- =installed-builtins-hooks-do-not-reach-the-cador-suite= installs the
  builtins, checks the leak source is live (=%wrap-com-point= returns a
  VARIANT out there), then checks that inside the cador suite's
  environment =%wrap-com-point= / =%wrap-com-objects= return plain lists
  and every hook is NIL. With the harness reverted to a bare =funcall= it
  fails 3 of its 6 checks.
- =without-builtin-layer-hooks-restores-the-installed-hooks= checks the
  macro unbinds rather than uninstalls (also across a THROW).

Acceptance criterion met: the cador suite passes after a suite that
installs the builtins (the tool suite, at load time, on every run).
=make test-sbcl= and =make test-ccl=: 34 suite runs each, Fail 0;
alfe =test-sbcl=: Fail 0.

Found on the way: =cador-tests-reference-builtins-core-without-depending-on-it.issue=.
